spinney.providers.markdownDescription:
OpenAI-compatible endpoints for the model cards, as structured data. Edit them in [settings.json](command:workbench.action.openSettingsJson?%7B%22revealSetting%22%3A%7B%22key%22%3A%22spinney.providers%22%2C%22edit%22%3Atrue%7D%7D) — or in the **Model Cards** page, which draws one node per provider and opens from the gear button beside the chat's model dropdown.

```json
"spinney.providers": {
  "deepseek": { "name": "DeepSeek", "baseUrl": "https://api.deepseek.com", "concurrency": 4 }
}
```

A provider is one endpoint: requests go to `POST <baseUrl>/chat/completions`, and `concurrency` caps how many of them may be in flight at once (0 = unlimited). The built-in `default` provider is always available; a row with that id replaces it. Every card names a provider id. Rows that cannot be parsed are ignored and listed in the **Spinney** output channel.
